      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "**Do not put milk in your eye; this is a dangerous myth and will likely irritate the chemical further.** Milk is not a neutralizer for industrial degreasers and could introduce infection or further chemical reaction. Since the stinging is fading, continue to flush your eye gently with cool water for a few more minutes, but if the irritation remains, you must find a way to see a healthcare provider. In some cases, you can call a local health advice line for guidance before committing to a long trip.",
